  "worked_solution": "The volume of the sphere is given by \n\n$$\nV=V(r)=\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $V(r)$ with respect to $r$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}^{\u2032}(r) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}r}(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}r}(\\pi {r}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot 3\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =4\\pi {r}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
